        "agenerateor": {
          "replies": [
            "For a backyard office with 420 square feet of exterior wall area at a thickness of 10 inches, your planning material volume is 9.9 cubic metres. \n\nSince speed is your top priority and you want to minimize hands-on mixing, pre-cast hemp-lime blocks are the best fit for your project. Pre-cast blocks arrive at your site already factory-cured, so you can lay them like standard masonry with a thin lime mortar. Once laid, the mortar dries in roughly two to three days, allowing you to move on to plastering and finishing much faster than you would with a cast-in-situ approach. \n\nWould you like to explore what the drying timeline and finishing steps look like for pre-cast blocks on your backyard office?"
